      {
        "text": "Richard P. Montgomery is a former four-term Manhattan Beach City Council member and mayor, having served from 2005 to 2013 and from 2017 to 2024. He works as a government affairs manager for an outdoor advertising company. He is a former reserve police officer. He supports halting the hiring of unnecessary city staff and restoring $9.5 million he says was removed from city reserves. He wants to prioritize enforcing anti-camping, anti-panhandling and electric-bike laws, and building a new downtown parking garage. He says he led the passage of a 2018 anti-camping ordinance that he credits with helping reduce the unhoused population from 41 to seven.",
